    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41342#issuecomment-5309279817\n\n> > is anything blocking us from hosting the result on https://neovim.io/ (static website)\n> \n> Yes, the demo needs `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` before browsers expose `SharedArrayBuffer`. But, Ig we could add the `coi-serviceworker` shim to spoof the headers client-side or host the demo on a platform that supports custom headers and link to it from neovim.io.\n\ncc @Rawan10101",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "## What's blocking hosting the WASM demo on neovim.io?\n\nThe WASM demo requires browser shared-memory support (`SharedArrayBuffer`). Browsers only expose `SharedArrayBuffer` when the page is **cross-origin isolated**.\n\nThat normally requires these HTTP response headers:\n\n```http\nCross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin\nCross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp\n```\n\n\n\nSimply copying the generated `.wasm`, JS, and HTML files onto a static website isn't enough. The server/CDN serving the page needs to attach those headers.\n\n`Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` also restricts cross-origin resources: external scripts, images, etc. generally need to explicitly opt in via CORS or `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy`.\n\nSo enabling these headers globally for `neovim.io` could potentially break existing externally hosted resources.\n\n## Options\n\n1. **Configure COOP/COEP headers.** Ideally only a path such as: `/wasm/**` would get the required headers, leaving the rest of `neovim.io` unchanged.\n    - depends on whether the host supports per-path custom HTTP response headers.\n2. **Use `coi-serviceworker`.**  Use a service worker to make cross-origin isolation work on static hosting where the server doesn't allow configuring the required headers. AKA \"spoof the headers client-side\".\n3. Host the demo elsewhere.\n\n",
